Theorem TF-14: Project backward demand propagation (well-definedness + QTT-consistency)

  Preconditions:
    - TF-14 propagate_project_source_demand mutates the source variable's
      AimsState in response to demand accumulated at the destination
      (projected) variable per Annex E §AIMS TF-14
    - Mutations:
        src.locality := max(src.locality, dst.locality)
        src.cardinality := seq_add(src.cardinality, dst.cardinality)
        src.consumption := seq_add(src.consumption, Affine)
    - L-9 excludes a scalar Project destination from AimsState. Its source-side
      RawDemand is therefore selected by scalarProjectContribution(live):
        live = false -> (Absent, Affine), the existing deadProjection
        live = true  -> (Once, Affine), one scalar copy-out occurrence
      The live contribution is capped at Once regardless of downstream scalar
      reuse or copy count; those scalar operations do not multiply the Project
      instruction's one copy-out from its managed source.
    - Scalar liveness is a separate two-point producer domain, not an AimsState
      dimension: dead < live, join = Boolean OR, and sparse-set absence = dead.
      Reverse alias transfer joins destination liveness into the source before
      killing the destination definition. A Jump edge performs the same
      substitution positionally from each target parameter to its argument,
      then kills the target parameter.
    - The scalar producer is monotone. Its carrier has height one (no two
      consecutive strict rises), so every monotone coordinate transfer seeded
      at dead reaches a fixed point after its only possible rise and remains
      stable on every later iteration.
    - The sole producer-to-demand seam is exact:
        ScalarLiveness.projectContribution(state)
          = RawDemand.scalarProjectContribution(state.toBool)
      No scalar value enters RawDemand or AimsState before that observation.
    - `seq_add` (not `max`) on Cardinality is QTT-consistent — a use through
      a projection counts as a use on the source, not a max-merged use.
      Using `max` would undercount when source and dst both have cardinality
      Once: max(Once, Once) = Once, but the projection's use AND the
      source's own direct use both consume the resource — actual cardinality
      is Many. Per Annex E §AIMS TF-14 statement.
    - No Access promotion at TF-14 (Owned promotion lives at IA-5 step (1)
      for `Set`-target value-promotion + escape-instructions); TF-14 leaves
      src.access UNCHANGED.
    - Composes with Annex E §AIMS project_alias_sources Rules 1 + 6
      (BORROW aliases only — non-BORROW R2/R3/R5/R7 aliases do NOT trigger
      propagate_project_source_demand)
    - L-6 monotonicity: TF-14 SHALL be monotone in dst.{cardinality,
      locality, consumption} for fixed src; AND monotone in src for fixed
      dst (the §3 TF-14 mutation is read-modify-write — both arguments
      monotone per L-6).

  Soundness property:
    Forall src, dst in AimsState.
      out := propagate_project_source_demand(src, dst) produces output
      with the three mutations per spec
    AND dst.locality1 <=_L dst.locality2 implies out_with(dst1).locality
        <=_L out_with(dst2).locality (monotone over dst.locality)
    AND dst.cardinality1 <=_K dst.cardinality2 implies
        out_with(dst1).cardinality <=_K out_with(dst2).cardinality
    AND out.access = src.access (no promotion)
    AND src.consumption increments by seq_add with Affine (NOT propagated
        from dst — independent of dst.consumption)
    AND ScalarLiveness.ProducerDomainLaws holds: join is Bool OR;
        transfer-before-kill and Jump-param substitution are monotone and
        identical pointwise; the height-one fixed point converges; and the
        producer-to-RawDemand seam is exact
    AND scalarProjectContribution(false) = deadProjection
    AND forall dst with dst.cardinality = Once,
        scalarProjectContribution(true) = projectContribution(dst)
    AND forall downstream scalar demand, scalarProjectContribution(true)
        remains (Once, Affine), independent of downstream copy count.

  Proof obligation:
    Six-part discharge:
      (a) Spec compliance — verify the three mutations exactly per §3 TF-14
          over a representative enumeration of (src, dst) pairs.
      (b) QTT-consistency — verify `seq_add` (not `max`) on Cardinality
          via the cardinality (Once, Once) -> Many witness; verify the
          undercount via the `max` alternative.
      (c) No-Access-promotion — verify out.access = src.access regardless
          of dst.access or src.access.
      (d) Monotonicity — enumerate the L-6 layer (b) check on dst.locality
          and dst.cardinality over their carriers.
      (e) Scalar producer — prove the dead/live order, Bool-OR join,
          transfer-before-kill, positional Jump-param substitution,
          monotonicity, height-one convergence, and exact RawDemand seam.
      (f) Scalar copy-out — prove live/dead liveness selection, equality with
          a managed Once destination, and the Once copy-out cap after replacing
          any downstream cardinality with the one-copy witness.

    Part (a) — spec compliance:
      Pick representative (src, dst) pairs over Locality x Cardinality x
      Consumption x Access and verify:
        out.locality == max_L(src.locality, dst.locality)
        out.cardinality == seq_add_K(src.cardinality, dst.cardinality)
        out.consumption == seq_add_C(src.consumption, Affine)
        out.access == src.access
        out.uniqueness == src.uniqueness (no propagation)
        out.shape == src.shape (no propagation)
        out.effect == src.effect (no propagation)

    Part (b) — QTT-consistency:
      Witness: src.cardinality = Once, dst.cardinality = Once.
        seq_add_K(Once, Once) = Many (correct — count of uses is 2)
        max_K(Once, Once) = Once (incorrect — undercount)
      Verified: tf14_qtt_witness() returns Many (not Once) confirming
      the seq_add path.

    Part (c) — no-Access-promotion:
      Enumerate src.access in {Borrowed, Owned} x dst.access in
      {Borrowed, Owned}:
        out.access = src.access for all 4 combinations
      Verified: tf14_no_access_promotion() returns the unchanged src.access
      regardless of dst.access. Negative witness — if Access were promoted
      to Owned, CN-8's Borrowed-locality clamp would not fire (CN-8 only
      applies to Borrowed) and downstream RC analysis would mis-emit.

    Part (d) — monotonicity:
      L-6 layer (b) on dst:
        forall src in AimsState. forall l1, l2 in LOCALITY_CARRIER.
          l1 <=_L l2 implies max_L(src.locality, l1) <=_L max_L(src.locality, l2)
        forall src. forall k1, k2 in CARDINALITY_CARRIER.
          k1 <=_K k2 implies seq_add_K(src.cardinality, k1) <=_K
                              seq_add_K(src.cardinality, k2)
      Both follow from monotonicity of `max` and `seq_add` over their
      respective lattices per L-6 layer (a) (proven at §02).
      Verified: 5 x 5 = 25 locality pairs x 5 src.locality values = 125
      cases for locality monotonicity; 3 x 3 = 9 cardinality pairs x 3
      src.cardinality values = 27 cases for cardinality monotonicity.

    Part (e) — scalar-liveness producer domain:
      ScalarLiveness.toBool/ofBool are inverse, so the formal dead/live carrier
      is exactly the sparse side table's Boolean membership coordinate.
      join_is_bool_or proves alternative-path union pointwise; join_comm,
      join_assoc, join_idem, join_dead_left, and below_iff_join_eq_right prove
      the bounded join-semilattice laws and its induced dead < live order.
      reverseTransfer joins destination into source before kill; its dead/live
      witnesses and reverseTransfer_monotone prove the reverse walk.
      jumpParamSubstitution applies the same operation to one zipped
      argument/target-param pair, kills the parameter, and is monotone.
      strictBelow_iff_dead_live and no_two_strict_rises prove carrier height
      one. monotone_from_dead_reaches_fixed_point and height_one_convergence
      prove every positive iteration is the same fixed point.
      projectContribution_exact_seam proves the only output consumed by TF-14
      is RawDemand.scalarProjectContribution(liveness.toBool).
      producer_domain_sound packages these obligations as ProducerDomainLaws.

    Part (f) — scalar Project copy-out:
      scalarProjectContribution(false) is definitionally deadProjection.
      For every managed destination with cardinality Once,
      scalarProjectContribution(true) equals projectContribution(destination).
      For an arbitrary downstream destination, replacing only its cardinality
      with Once yields the same live scalar contribution. This is the copy-out
      cap: downstream scalar reuse cannot promote the source Project to Many.
      TF14_scalar_project_copy_out_sound discharges all three clauses, and
      TF14_project_demand_sound composes them with ProducerDomainLaws and
      managed propagation.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) on dst.locality + dst.cardinality
        per section_04::verify_tf14_project_propagation)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — spec-compliance + QTT-consistency +
        no-Access-promotion enumeration per
        section_04::verify_tf14_project_propagation)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; max + seq_add monotone per L-6
        layer (a))
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-14 does NOT call refine())

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-14 via the scalar dead/live Bool-OR producer, transfer-before-kill, Jump-param substitution, height-one convergence, exact RawDemand seam, managed spec-compliance, scalar live/dead copy-out cap, QTT-consistency, no-Access-promotion, and L-6 monotonicity enumeration on dst.locality + dst.cardinality
